Now I made the plot for Holly's Joyful Holiday, (the Snow Day remake). 
Plot:
When it's not snowing on Joyful Holiday, Holly must find a quick way to deliver all her presents to her friends. Suddenly Peanut, Spot and Jewel arrive where the latter offers to help. Holly plans to deliver the presents by sleigh when it snows all over Lalaloopsy Land, as it still doesn't snow along with the green areas overlapping more than normal, she Holly can't leave. Holly meanwhile asks the showgirls to practice. Dot calls and reports that the weather hasn't changed in Lalaloopsy Land. Peanut then offers to give her a ride in her clown car, but Holly declines out of tradition.
Holly, taking advantage of the fact that there is still snow, is going to deliver gifts to the mittens house. where she last mentions that she has a plan to help her. Back with Holly, she stumbles when she reaches the green area. Holly delivers the dOT gifts, and she offers to deliver them by plane to which Holly refuses. Dot offers to help her by putting a sheet under the sled and they go to Forest's house. On the way through the woods, the sled gets stuck in the mud. With Forest helping the girls who puts wooden wheels on the sled and offers to help. While they were going through the snowy area of Lalaloopsy Land to Rosy's house, the sleigh derails and goes down the hill. The snow covers up the sleigh even more. The Schwartzman Quartet enters, singing "Sing a Christmas Song."
Near Rosy's hospital, she hears a crash and goes with her medical kit for help where she partially repairs the sled. Rosy also joins the cause where she starts to snow heavily. The girls go to Patch's house and the crumbs house, bea. The girls leave the sled behind and head off walking but end up spinning in circles. Holly is sorry for her because she decided to get out of it in this weather and for bringing her friends with her.
Mittens, after deducing that Holly will take a long time to deliver the gifts, goes to her house to practice with the showgirls on how to sing the song, but Spot sings out of tune. Mittens gives in and subtly tells him to ring the bells. Jewel then begins to give a couple of problems asking for a candy for the throat, a cup of tea, improvising alone. The girls sing again but they sing very loud, especially Peanut. The girls, noticing the strong wind, go in search of Holly using a long blue scarf.
Things were getting bad for both groups, it was getting dark and pessimism was beginning to take hold of the lalas. So they decide to sing the Christmas carol to cheer up the spirits. Forest meanwhile listens to the Christmas carol and thought it was the wind, but then they notice that it was Peanut because of the screams he was making. Holly's group responds with the same Christmas carol so they can meet up. It suddenly stops snowing, they meet, and Mittens hugs Holly. The girls express how good it felt to help Holly. The story concludes with the lalas again singing the carol as a group with Crumbs, Bea and Crumbs joining in at the last minute.
